    desc: "Cybergoth codified in late-1990s Europe as goth met rave and industrial dance music, and it answers traditional goth's black-only palette with neon UV accents. The kit: cyberlox and brightly coloured dreadfalls, goggles and respirator masks, PVC and fishnet layers, platform New Rock boots, and ultraviolet-reactive details made for blacklit clubs. The soundtrack is EBM and futurepop — VNV Nation, Covenant, Combichrist — with its own bounce-driven club dance. Camden Market's Cyberdog store became the style's flagship retailer, and the look was documented by the Consumer Aesthetics Research Institute as a distinct consumer aesthetic. In the 2010s the 'cybergoth dance' video meme spread the silhouette worldwide; today the style persists in industrial club nights and as a nostalgic fashion reference within 2000s revivals.",
