    p: "c. 2018–2022", era: "Instagram and TikTok retail trend cycle",
    sum: "Smiley flowers, checkerboards and wavy pastel prints: the mass-produced arty-surface fashion CARI named 'avant basics'.",
    desc: "Avant basic is the Consumer Aesthetics Research Institute's name for the 2018–2022 wave of fast fashion that dressed basic silhouettes in loud, playful surface design: pink smiley faces, daisies, checkerboards that warp and drip, flame prints and clashing pastels. Retailers from Urban Outfitters and Zara to online-native labels like Lisa Says Gah churned the prints; House of Sunny's green checkerboard cardigan became the wave's breakout product around 2020, circulated endlessly on Instagram and TikTok. The aesthetic reads as trend cycle speed itself — surfaces recycled from 1960s-70s psychedelia and Memphis-era geometry, produced at fast-fashion velocity, mocked as 'SHEIN psychedelic' even as it sold. It waned around 2022 into coquette and indie-sleaze revivals, remaining a textbook case of a design institute naming a trend after the fact.",
    col: [{ h: "#f7b5d9", n: "pink smile" }, { h: "#7ee081", n: "grass green" }, { h: "#ffec6e", n: "daisy yellow" }, { h: "#ffffff", n: "checker white" }, { h: "#2a2a2a", n: "contrast black" }],
