    desc: "Mermaidcore peaked in 2023, coinciding with Disney's live-action The Little Mermaid (May 2023), as TikTok and retail converged on sea-maiden dressing: sequined scale prints, iridescent and wet-look slip fabrics, shell and pearl jewellery, aqua-to-teal gradients and coral accents. Mermaid imagery has older fashion lineages — from 1930s bias-cut 'mermaid gown' silhouettes through art-nouveau siren illustration and 1990s iridescent clubwear — which the trend re-cut into beach-adjacent, festival-ready styling. Lookbooks paired scale-print minis with pearl layers and wet-look slicked hair; press coverage framed it alongside coquette and mermaid-adjacent 'siren' editorial. As with other TikTok cores, its lifecycle was short and retail-driven, but the iridescent-mesh look stayed resident in clubwear and swim collections.",
