    sum: "Fringed vests, floaty maxis and layered jewellery: the Sienna Miller-era bohemian revival that turned hippie dress into mall fashion.",
    desc: "Boho chic revived hippie and prairie dress through a celebrity street-style lens: Sienna Miller's 2004 Glastonbury appearance — ugg boots, fringed waistcoat, messy braids — and Kate Moss's mid-2000s looks became the templates, and Topshop-era retail industrialised the formula of floaty peasant skirts, suede waistcoats, floppy hats, layered necklaces and flats. The Wikipedia article on boho-chic documents the trend's reach and its critics, who charged that romanticized 'bohemian' poverty was sold at luxury prices to festival crowds. Its elements recycle genuinely: 1960s hippie dress, 1970s prairie revivals and older gypsy-romantic clichés flattened into one palette of sun-washed neutrals and terracotta embroidery. By the early 2010s the wave crested, but festival fashion kept the silhouette alive, and 'boho' remains a standing retail category.",
